here in this video we shall try to get  to the bottom of a very ancient question  one that has been floating around for  millions of years and that is which is  the most powerful dinosaur in the  jurassic franchise is it the spinosaurus  the indominus rex or the giganotosaurus  sorry rexy fans but these three dinos  have defeated the t-rex in their  separate appearances in the jurassic  franchise but they haven't faced each  other so let's get down to solving this  question  we shall first take a look at their  battles and we will be assessing their  powers by watching them battle with the  t-rex let's start with the first dino vs  dino the spinosaurus t-rex battle as you  can see in jurassic park 3 the battle  was shot lasting for roughly 30 seconds  even though the t-rex got the first bite  on the neck of the spiner the ladder was  undoubtedly more powerful and shrugged  off it was also unfazed by the headbutts  of the t-rex and then it delivered a  neck-breaking bite of its own with the  help of its longer hands holding onto  the wrecks as it snaps it killing the  t-rex instantly  then we shift to the next battle between  the big carnivals the t-rex was released  from its enclosure in the wake of the  indominus rex causing chaos in the park  the two squared off against one another  and it would be the first time the irex  faced off against another apex predator  the bell lasted for around 40 to 50  seconds just under a minute and although  rexy initially got the upper hand in a  shock attack the irex counter-attack and  pummeled the t-rex into submission but  just before it was about to deliver the  killing blow blue the raptor intervened  and turned the tide of the battle in  rexy's favor  and so in the latest confrontation the  t-rex and the giganotosaurus fought in  the newly released prologue for jurassic  world dominion they kinda had this short  face-off with them walking around kind  of like an intimidation display and  roared at each other the t-rex tried to  get into the giga's neck but the gigger  fended off that attack with a headboard  of its own they smashed into one another  struggling with a scene showing the giga  nearly falling off into a ravine but  then in a short time the giganotosaurus  got the upper hand bit the t-rex's neck  and maybe it would have snapped it like  the way the spino did and yieted the  t-rex into the ravine sealing the fate  of rexy in a measly 22nd battle  now let's assess the advantages and  disadvantages for each dinosaur starting  with the spinosaurus it was undoubtedly  the biggest carnivore in the jurassic  franchise being about 52 feet long and  weighed eight tons its main advantage  against t-rex was its speed agility and  size as well as its longer forearms  which it used to deadly effect while  snapping the buck t-rex's neck it would  have had more advantage if the battle  was near a water source because it is a  semi-aquatic species the main  disadvantage though is the big sail like  spine which would be a big target and a  vulnerable area for bites  now the indo wrecks advantages and  disadvantages well the disadvantages for  this hybrid is few and far in between i  could not think of one as it is created  for to be a perfect predator but i could  see that it would be vulnerable around  water sources and swamps as it was  killed by the mosasaurus its main  advantages would be its high  intelligence owing to the fact that it  has wrapped the genes in it it could  camouflage and blend to any surrounding  therefore making it a perfect ambush  predator it also has tough skin and a  pair of longer forearms and a jaw that  could deliver a powerful bite force due  to the genes of the t-rex infused in it  and lastly the giganotosaurus well not  much is known about this dino except for  the fact that it is bigger than the  t-rex so it would have been between 45  and 50 feet long it also has bigger  forearms but not by much as compared to  the irex and the spinosaurus it does  however have a tough semi-armored skin  which we can see by its big osteodomes  on its back and scaly crocodilian skin  it also has a powerful bite force with  serrated dagger-like teeth it might also  have the added characteristic of brute  strength as seen with it killing the  t-rex in 20 seconds and kicking it to  the curb afterwards  so in conclusion all three dinosaurs are  extremely powerful and hence why ranking  them is so difficult but judging by the  battle against the t-rex and the giga  took the lead with a win in under 20  seconds as compared to 30 for the spino  and around 50 for the irex but if we  look at the advantages and disadvantages  comparison the indominus rex takes the  lead in many areas such as intelligence  camouflage and overall flexibility the  spiner takes to win for size and would  be king if any battle is fought near a  swamp or a water source but overall i  would have to say that in an open field  battle or an arena-like condition where  there's no external factor  that would help one or the other i think  that the indominus rex would win the  fight against either the spinal or the  giga and i think that the spiner would  win against the giganotosaurus so there  we have it the irex then the spino then  the giganotosaurus then t-rex  and so with that we come to the end of  the video do hit that like button for  support and click on that subscribe  button as well to be a part of the mind  care family but most of all smash that  bell icon for regular updates on new  videos right here on this channel till  the next one take care fam
 

